      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8ddc12e0",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "attention_seeking_behavior",
      "label": "Attention-Seeking Behavior",
      "description": "The meme uses the concept of 'attention-seeking' as a social stereotype or behavioral label, often applied pejoratively to describe individuals who are perceived as overly eager to be noticed or admired. This concept is not visible in the image but is central to the meme's sarcastic tone — implying that joining the circus is an 'attention-seeking' act, which is ironically framed as an invitation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_326ebe9f",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "circus_as_attention_grabber",
      "label": "Circus as a Symbol of Spectacle and Attention",
      "description": "Circuses are culturally recognized as venues of spectacle, performance, and entertainment designed to capture and hold public attention. This cultural understanding is necessary to interpret the meme’s irony — the performers are literally seeking attention, and the meme sarcastically invites the viewer to join them, implying that the event is inherently attention-grabbing.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f8f3a9f2",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "sarcastic_invitation",
      "label": "Sarcastic Invitation",
      "description": "The meme relies on the rhetorical device of sarcasm — using an ironic or mocking tone to invite participation. This requires background knowledge of how sarcasm functions in communication, particularly in internet culture, where such ironic invitations are common in memes to create humor or provoke engagement.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_10cfae23",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "public_event_promotion",
      "label": "Public Event Promotion",
      "description": "The meme functions as a form of promotional content, leveraging the visual context of a live performance to attract attendees. This requires understanding that such images are often used in marketing or advertising to generate interest in real-world events, which is the underlying intent of the meme’s overall intent.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7ef06bb0",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "audience_as_consumer",
      "label": "Audience as Passive Consumer",
      "description": "The image depicts an audience seated and watching, which implies a passive consumption of entertainment. This reflects a cultural understanding of how audiences interact with live performances — as spectators rather than active participants — which is essential to interpreting the meme’s invitation to 'join us' as ironic or performative.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f7011a22",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "circus_performance_as_entertainment",
      "label": "Circus Performance as Entertainment",
      "description": "The concept that circus performances are a form of entertainment designed to amuse and captivate audiences is a cultural norm. This background knowledge is necessary to understand why the performers are 'looking for attention' — because that is the very nature of their profession and the purpose of the event.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_05cc2715",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "sarcastic_irony",
      "label": "sarcastic and ironic tone",
      "description": "The text overlay 'looking for attention? join us' expresses a sarcastic and ironic invitation, implying that joining the circus is an attention-seeking act, which is humorously framed as a call to action. This emotion is conveyed through the juxtaposition of the literal spectacle of the circus (where performers inherently seek attention) with the mocking tone of the invitation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c0937fa2",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "audience as attention-seeking participants",
      "description": "The text 'looking for attention?' is mapped onto the visual entity 'audience', implying that the audience is the one seeking attention by attending the circus. This is ironic, as the audience is passive consumers, but the text sarcastically frames their presence as attention-seeking behavior, aligning with the performers' inherent attention-seeking nature.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bb8b791a",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the audience as attention-seeking participants",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the audience, as the text 'looking for attention? join us' sarcastically implies that the viewer (user) is being invited to join the attention-seeking behavior of the performers and the audience. The projection is onto the visual material of the audience, who are depicted as passive consumers, but the text frames their presence as attention-seeking, creating an ironic invitation. This aligns with the mapping where the audience is analogically mapped as attention-seeking participants.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_039808ad"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
